Put a directory named after the Arch pkgbase here (overrides/<pkgbase>/PKGBUILD
plus any patches / .install files) to replace the official Arch PKGBUILD for
that module. build.sh still rewrites its git sources to the drive and
generates pkgver(), so keep the upstream repo in source=() as a git+ URL.

Typical reasons: an Arch patch no longer applies to main, the official
package is built from a release tarball, or you want extra meson options.
